& [IdentityAudit] passes
  + preserved source bytes and SHA256 match its manifest
  + every named canonical input and current integration file was measured at the baseline
  + every proposed implementation module was absent at the baseline

& [SourceRole] is manager-derived formation input
  + it consolidates already formed source-touch intentions and an observed collision audit
  + it is not dictated implementation authority
  + canonical processing may refine ambiguity but cannot silently expand the source boundary

& [AuthorityAudit] refuses implementation
  + I02C completion is a valid predecessor fact
  + I03 through I03E3 remain formation-only or unsigned candidates with zero implementation and verification counts
  + no activation lease exists merely because this source names one
  + Enterprise signing denial and absent jsonschema lock prevent I03A activation
  + E3 trust policy and authorized reviewer catalogue are absent

& [Delineation1] activation queue order differs from hard compile dependency
  + A before B is a governance serialization choice that keeps one auditable path
  + D has hard semantic dependencies on A B and C
  + E1 has a hard post-D identity dependency
  + E2 E3 and E have hard causal dependencies stated by their own specifications
  + the canonical form must label dependency edges as governance_order or hard_prerequisite

& [Delineation2] source ownership differs from shared-file custody
  + a semantic owner authors one exclusive module and focused test
  + an integration steward applies declaration and re-export deltas to shared ledgers
  + stewardship cannot change module semantics or substitute for the owning phase signature
  + shared ledger authorship and semantic implementation authorship remain separately attributable

& [Delineation3] a TouchLease is prospective formation
  + the source defines a future lease record shape
  + no current lease or executor authority is created
  + a future issued lease requires an active phase lock exact predecessor and bounded delta
  + stale or mismatched predecessors refuse rather than auto-merge

& [Delineation4] satisfaction signature differs from digital signature
  + a satisfaction signature is the governed project record that closes exact requirements under the framework
  + a digital signature is cryptographic verification under algorithm key and trust catalogue
  + I03E3 may require cryptographic signatures for review artifacts under a future policy
  + no present record should call an integrity digest or faculty signoff a cryptographic signature

& [Delineation5] fixture root differs from fixture inventory
  + tests/fixtures/cpms_i03 is a proposed organizational root
  + it is not an admitted path until a future source and activation lock enumerate it
  + directory naming does not grant runtime discovery or mutable-corpus authority
  + every admitted fixture remains a complete content-addressed record

& [Delineation6] parent report formation precedes child implementation only in documentation time
  + I03E was canonically formed before E1 E2 and E3
  + executable report assembly must occur after D E1 E2 and E3 completion
  + formation chronology cannot invert runtime dependency authority

& [Correction1] integration ledgers may contain declarations cfg gates and re-exports only
  + constants implementations validation logic review rules and corpus policy belong in exclusive modules
  + this keeps shared-file conflict surface mechanical and reviewable

& [Correction2] one active unit at a time is a default safety policy not an assertion that all implementation must be single-threaded
  + disjoint research tests fixtures and exclusive modules may be prepared in parallel only when authority and prerequisites allow
  + shared surfaces and causal outputs remain serialized
  + this formation used no subagent or external worker

& [Correction3] completion is exact
  + source mutation test passage or commit presence alone is not completion
  + completion requires every unit requirement implemented verified reviewed satisfaction-signed and bound by an active phase lock
  + downstream identities bind the completed predecessor rather than a working-tree approximation

& [Correction4] host admission is temporal evidence
  + a future successful execution does not erase the preserved Enterprise-signing denial
  + the exact rebuilt artifact environment policy and command must be observed
  + present formation cannot predict that a future binary will be admitted

& [Correction5] rollback language is non-destructive
  + repository history and failed attempts remain evidence
  + recovery selects or reconstructs a reviewed predecessor through a successor commit
  + no reset deletion or history rewrite is prescribed

& [DualHemisphereGenerative] supports
  + small responsibility-aligned modules
  + mirrored tests and content-addressed fixtures
  + worker partition by exclusive ownership
  + deterministic integration receipts and dependency reconstruction

& [DualHemisphereCritical] attacks
  + documentary-candidate laundering into active prerequisites
  + stale shared-file merges
  + module ownership overlap and semantic logic hidden in ledgers
  + partial activation and downstream execution after failed units
  + signature terminology collapse fixture mutation and host-proof overclaim

& [SJSDecision] is canonical formation permitted with implementation refused
  + retain eight activation units A B C D E1 E2 E3 and E
  + retain one semantic owner per exclusive module
  + introduce typed dependency edges and prospective lease records
  + require future exact fixture inventory and trust inputs
  + preserve all blockers and zero I03 implementation counts

& [AuditDisposition] is SJS_input_accepted_for_topology_formation_only
